.TH ZERO 4 "February 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
zero \- zero-byte source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/zero
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B zero
character device returns an endless stream of null bytes (0x00) on read.
.PP
Writes to
.B /dev/zero
are accepted and discarded, returning the requested byte count.
.PP
.BR lseek (2)
operations succeed and update file offsets, but offsets do not affect read/write behavior.
.PP
.BR poll (2)
reports both
.B POLLIN
and
.B POLLOUT
as ready.
.BR ioctl (2)
is not supported.
.PP
.BR mmap (2)
of
.B /dev/zero
is supported and returns zero-filled memory.
.SH FILES
.B /dev/zero
(character device, major 1, minor 5)
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOTTY
Any
.BR ioctl (2)
request.
.SH EXAMPLE
Create a 1 MiB zero-filled file:
.PP
.nf
    $ dd if=/dev/zero of=zeros.bin bs=1M count=1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR null (4),
.BR full (4),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR poll (2)
